<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 5.008 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 5.008 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Thursday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one week and four weeks, yielding 3.79 percent and 17.74 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 5.008 billion levs of T-bills and the ministry approved all of them.</p>
<p>The issues were offered with no par values or minimum acceptable prices set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3015097002	 BG3015197000</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  February 13, 1997  February 13, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 13, 1997  February 13, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 20, 1997  March 13, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 3,608 million levs     1,400 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.35 pct	    84.93</p>
<p> Bids approved		 3,608 million levs     1,400 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.35 pct	    84.93 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.79 pct	     17.74 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
